Z||000000||mrfiero||05-21-2000||02:11 AM||||This is a little late for me to be asking this (I leave for a trip in 7 hours), but I need to know if a tow dolly requires a license plate/registration.  Does anyone know for sure?<P>I am borrowing a friends dolly and it doesn't have a plate.  I have asked several people and most say it isn't required.  I'm just looking for any other thoughts or inputs on this, since I'll be driving from Denver to Maine....I don't want to get pulled over in every state!<P>Thanks.<BR>  <P> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||phillip||05-21-2000||05:53 AM||||i rented a truck and tow dolly from u-haul last weekend. the dolly had no plate. rented fron ind. to ky. it was one of their one way pices so i guess it ends up any where in the country. don't know if u-haul has a special deal though. by the way, it was to pick up my indy i got off ebay a few weeks back . finaly have it home.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||05-21-2000||10:35 AM||||Thanks.  It seems that different states have different requirements for tow dollies....which makes no sense to me.  The majority say their state doesn't require one, so I'm going to risk it!  :-)<P>Thanks again.||||reg||7
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-21-2000||01:10 PM||||Towed the Grape Ape from Wheaton, Ill  (Chicago suburb) to central Indiana.  U-Haul tow dolly, no plates.  Didn't have a problem (except for the snow and the fact that the tow vehicles ABS didn't work once!).||||reg||1
